{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "title": "LLM Pulse API",
    "description": "REST API for the LLM Pulse AI visibility platform. Track brand mentions, citations, sentiment, and Share of Voice across AI-generated answers (ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini, Google AI Overviews, Google AI Mode, and optional add-on models). Includes the MCP (Model Context Protocol) endpoint for AI clients. MCP is available on every plan and during eligible trials via OAuth 2.1, with Bearer-token API keys also accepted for headless integrations on the Scale plan or above. Full machine-readable reference at https://llmpulse.ai/api-docs/llms-full.txt. An API key can be limited to one or several projects when it is created, and the set never changes. Such a key sees only those projects: any other project id, domain or name answers ERR_PROJECT_NOT_FOUND exactly like a project that does not exist, listings return only those projects' rows, and operations on the whole account (creating a project, the project draft wizard) answer ERR_KEY_PROJECT_SCOPED. Operations carry vendor extensions: x-plan is the plan or entitlement the endpoint requires beyond an API key (growth, scale or reputation_access), x-write marks endpoints that need a read and write key, x-mcp-tool names the MCP tool that returns the same data, x-mcp-plan gives that tool's plan where it differs, and x-rest-only explains an endpoint with no MCP tool.",
    "version": "1.60.0",
    "contact": {
      "name": "LLM Pulse Support",
      "url": "https://llmpulse.ai",
      "email": "info@llmpulse.ai"
    },
    "license": {
      "name": "Proprietary",
      "url": "https://llmpulse.ai/terms"
    }
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://api.llmpulse.ai/api/v1",
      "description": "Production API"
    }
  ],
  "security": [
    {
      "BearerAuth": []
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "description": "Health check that validates an API key and, optionally, access to a project."
    },
    {
      "name": "Account",
      "description": "Plan, subscription window, quota consumption and API rate limits for the authenticated account. Read it before spending quota so an integration can see its remaining budget instead of discovering the ceiling by hitting it."
    },
    {
      "name": "Projects",
      "description": "A project is one tracked brand. List and read projects, see which AI models and locales have data, create a project in one call, or drive the multi-step draft wizard."
    },
    {
      "name": "Metrics",
      "description": "Aggregated visibility, share of voice, citation and position data for the project and its competitors: time series, period summary, per-prompt summary, Share of Voice and top cited sources."
    },
    {
      "name": "Competitors",
      "description": "The brands tracked alongside your own. Competitor ids are the actor_id values the metrics endpoints report against."
    },
    {
      "name": "Prompts",
      "description": "The questions executed against the AI models every week, and the execution records each run produces."
    },
    {
      "name": "Collections & Tags",
      "description": "Collections (labelled Tags in the app) group prompts by topic, funnel stage or campaign so metrics can be filtered by them."
    },
    {
      "name": "Answers",
      "description": "The AI responses behind every metric, with their full text, mentions, citations and sentiment analysis."
    },
    {
      "name": "Mentions & Citations",
      "description": "The raw records behind the visibility metrics: one row per brand mention or per cited URL, for the project brand, for competitors, or for both in a single stream."
    },
    {
      "name": "Sentiments",
      "description": "Sentiment records with their comments, topics and scores, plus the category catalog used to label them."
    },
    {
      "name": "Sources & Citation Intelligence",
      "description": "Every URL extracted from AI responses, plus grouped URL, domain and host views, page-cache metadata, mention evidence inside cited pages, occurrences and sanitized cached content."
    },
    {
      "name": "AI Model Insights",
      "description": "Aggregate AI Model Insights report endpoints (summary, position distribution, AI Overview results). All filter by executed_at and share a standard actor shape."
    },
    {
      "name": "AI & Agent Traffic",
      "description": "What AI sends to your site: referral traffic from AI assistants measured by the connected web analytics provider, and AI crawler traffic hitting your origin server. Scale plan and above."
    },
    {
      "name": "Shopping & Ads",
      "description": "Commercial surfaces inside AI answers: the product cards models return, the paid placements that run alongside them, and the local businesses they list for prompts with local intent. Shopping and ads need the Scale plan or above; local businesses are available on every plan."
    },
    {
      "name": "Owned Media & Communities",
      "description": "Which of your own channels and which community conversations AI answers cite: YouTube, Instagram, Facebook, TikTok, LinkedIn, app-store listings and Reddit. Growth plan and above."
    },
    {
      "name": "Reputation & Studies",
      "description": "Multi-model analyst reports: the monthly reputation scoring of your brand against its competitors, and the custom AI studies you define over any subjects and dimensions. Requires reputation monitoring."
    },
    {
      "name": "Search Console",
      "description": "Google Search Console performance data (impressions, clicks, CTR, average position) for projects with a connected GSC property: headline totals, time series, top queries and top pages. Growth plan and above."
    },
    {
      "name": "Recommendations",
      "description": "Recommendation runs that power the in-app Recommendations page, plus the endpoint that launches a new one."
    },
    {
      "name": "GEO Writer",
      "description": "AI-powered GEO Writer tasks (formerly Content Intelligence). Tasks are processed asynchronously, so create one and poll it until it completes."
    },
    {
      "name": "Technical GEO Reports",
      "description": "Run the technical GEO analysis bundle, then list, poll and retrieve each completed report."
    },
    {
      "name": "GEO Audits",
      "description": "Audits re-run one technical GEO check type on a domain or URL, once or weekly/monthly. Each run is kept: compare runs check by check, follow issues across runs (new, fixed, regressed), accept known issues and read the alerts scheduled runs raised."
    },
    {
      "name": "Annotations",
      "description": "Mark a date on the project timeline (a campaign launch, a site migration) so charts show what happened when."
    },
    {
      "name": "Team",
      "description": "The account team: list members and pending invitations, invite someone by email with their projects and access, revoke an invitation or remove a member, with the same rules as the Team Members settings page. Not available to a key limited to some projects."
    },
    {
      "name": "Store Integrations",
      "description": "The endpoints behind the LLM Pulse app for Shopify: match a store to its project, push the orders AI assistants referred to the store and read them back, and turn catalog products into buyer prompts to track. They need an API key (Scale plan or above) and are not available to accounts with a white-label portal or an embed, which receive ERR_INTEGRATION_UNAVAILABLE (403)."
    },
    {
      "name": "Webhooks",
      "description": "Outbound event notifications: subscribe an HTTPS URL to project events and receive HMAC-signed deliveries with no polling. Scale plan and above."
    },
    {
      "name": "MCP",
      "description": "Model Context Protocol endpoint for AI clients (Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor and other MCP-compatible assistants)."
    },
    {
      "name": "OAuth 2.1",
      "description": "OAuth 2.1 authorization for MCP clients: discovery metadata, dynamic client registration, authorization, token exchange and JWKS."
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/ping": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Health"
        ],
        "summary": "Health check",
        "x-llms-description": "Health check; validates the API key and optionally pings a project.",
        "description": "Validates the API key and optionally pings a project. Returns the authenticated user_id, project (if project_id is supplied), and a request_id.",
        "operationId": "ping",
        "x-rest-only": "Key and project health check; an MCP client checks its connection with the initialize handshake.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "project_id",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "description": "Optional project to verify access for"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "API is healthy",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "ok": {
                      "type": "boolean"
                    },
                    "user_id": {
                      "type": "integer"
                    },
                    "project": {
                      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Project"
                    },
                    "request_id": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/account": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Account"
        ],
        "summary": "Account plan, quota usage and rate limits",
        "x-llms-description": "Plan, subscription window, quota usage (prompts, projects, competitors, intelligence tasks) and API rate limits for the authenticated account.",
        "description": "Returns the account plan, tracking cadence, subscription window, how much of each quota is used (prompts, projects, competitors per project, monthly GEO Writer tasks, team members, active recurring GEO audits and manual GEO audit runs in the last 24 hours) and the published API rate limits. Limits resolve through the account owner, so a team member sees the capacity that applies to them. An unlimited quota returns limit and remaining as null with unlimited set to true, since Infinity is not representable in JSON. The subscription block is only present for callers who can access Billing and Plans in the app (the account owner, or a team member with billing access); everyone else gets the same response without that key. requests_per_minute is the ceiling of the key used for the call, not a fixed number. For a key limited to some projects, the response carries nothing about the rest of the account: plan, plan_name, subscription and limits.team_members are absent, api_key_project_ids lists the key's projects, limits.prompts.used counts those projects' prompts, limits.prompts, limits.intelligence_tasks and the two GEO audit quotas show only remaining and unlimited (the capacity the key can still spend, without the account total), and the projects quota is capped at the projects it reaches. tracking_frequency stays, as the cadence those projects' data is collected at.",
        "operationId": "getAccount",
        "x-mcp-tool": "get_account_usage",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Account usage snapshot",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "plan": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "Plan key (starter, growth, scale, ...). Absent for a key limited to some projects."
                    },
                    "plan_name": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "Display name of the plan to show people (e.g. Scale++ for the scaleplusplus key). Absent for a key limited to some projects."
                    },
                    "tracking_frequency": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "How often prompts run (weekly, daily, monthly, ...)"
                    },
                    "role": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "enum": [
                        "owner",
                        "member"
                      ],
                      "description": "Whether the key belongs to the account owner or a team member"
                    },
                    "api_key_project_ids": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "type": "integer"
                      },
                      "nullable": true,
                      "description": "The projects the calling API key is limited to; null for a key that sees the whole account, and for OAuth"
                    },
                    "subscription": {
                      "type": "object",
                      "description": "Billing state. Present only for callers who can access Billing and Plans in the app; absent otherwise.",
                      "properties": {
                        "status": {
                          "type": "string"
                        },
                        "trialing": {
                          "type": "boolean"
                        },
                        "current_period_ends_at": {
                          "type": "string",
                          "format": "date-time",
                          "nullable": true
                        }
                      }
                    },
                    "limits": {
                      "type": "object",
                      "properties": {
                        "prompts": {
                          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AccountQuota"
                        },
                        "projects": {
                          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AccountQuota"
                        },
                        "competitors_per_project": {
                          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AccountCapacity"
                        },
                        "intelligence_tasks": {
                          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AccountQuota"
                        },
                        "team_members": {
                          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AccountCapacity"
                        },
                        "recurring_geo_audits": {
                          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AccountQuota"
                        },
                        "geo_audit_manual_runs": {
                          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AccountQuota"
                        }
                      }
                    },
                    "rate_limits": {
                      "type": "object",
                      "properties": {
                        "requests_per_minute": {
                          "type": "integer",
                          "description": "The ceiling enforced for the API key used on this call, which may be above the 300/min default."
                        },
                        "write_requests_per_minute": {
                          "type": "integer",
                          "description": "Flat ceiling on write requests, the same for every key."
                        }
                      }
                    },
                    "request_id": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/dimensions/projects": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Projects"
        ],
        "summary": "List projects",
        "x-llms-description": "List all projects accessible to the API key.",
        "operationId": "listProjects",
        "x-mcp-tool": "list_projects",
        "description": "All projects accessible with your API key.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Output"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Projects",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "projects": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Project"
                      }
                    },
                    "request_id": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/dimensions/projects/{id}": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Projects"
        ],
        "summary": "Project details",
        "x-llms-description": "Detailed info for one project: matching names, locale, industry, app store IDs, stats.",
        "operationId": "getProjectDetails",
        "x-mcp-tool": "get_project_details",
        "description": "Detailed info for one project: matching_names, additional_owned_domains, industry, business model, primary products, target audience, brand voice, locale, app store IDs, stats (incl. prompts_by_brand_kind counts) and data_coverage (models, countries and languages with data).",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "integer"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Project details",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProjectDetails"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/dimensions/models": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Projects"
        ],
        "summary": "List models with data",
        "x-llms-description": "List AI models the project has execution data for.",
        "operationId": "listModels",
        "x-mcp-tool": "list_models",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ProjectId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Models",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ModelsResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/dimensions/locales": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Projects"
        ],
        "summary": "List locales with data",
        "x-llms-description": "List countries and languages with data for the project.",
        "operationId": "listLocales",
        "x-mcp-tool": "list_locales",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ProjectId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Locales",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/LocalesResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/project_drafts": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "Projects"
        ],
        "summary": "Start a project draft (wizard step 1)",
        "x-llms-description": "Start the multi-step project wizard: returns a draft_id + AI suggestions for the URL (name, description, industry, aliases).",
        "operationId": "createProjectDraft",
        "x-mcp-tool": "start_project_draft",
        "x-write": true,
        "description": "Start the multi-step project-creation wizard. Returns a draft_id plus AI suggestions (name, description, industry, brand aliases) for the URL. Cold URLs can take up to ~2 minutes to analyze; pass suggest=false to skip AI and respond instantly. Drafts expire after 24h. Requires a `read_write` scope API key.",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "website_url",
                  "main_country",
                  "main_language"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "website_url": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "format": "uri",
                    "description": "Public HTTP(S) URL with a DNS hostname or public IP address. Credentials, private and special IP addresses, localhost and internal hostnames are rejected."
                  },
                  "main_country": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "main_language": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "use_subdomain": {
                    "type": "boolean",
                    "default": false
                  },
                  "suggest": {
                    "type": "boolean",
                    "default": true
                  },
                  "execute_prompts_immediately": {
                    "type": "boolean",
                    "default": true
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "Draft created; envelope with draft state, suggestions and limits"
          },
          "422": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/UnprocessableEntity"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/KeyProjectScoped"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/project_drafts/{id}": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Projects"
        ],
        "summary": "Read a project draft",
        "x-llms-description": "Read a draft: state, current step, accumulated data; include_suggestions=true returns cached suggestions only.",
        "operationId": "getProjectDraft",
        "x-mcp-tool": "get_project_draft",
        "x-write": true,
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": "Draft id (draft_...)"
          },
          {
            "name": "include_suggestions",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": {
              "type": "boolean",
              "default": false
            },
            "description": "Cache-only: returns suggestions for the current step if already generated, never triggers AI"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Draft envelope"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/KeyProjectScoped"
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
          }
        }
      },
      "patch": {
        "tags": [
          "Projects"
        ],
        "summary": "Submit a wizard step",
        "x-llms-description": "Submit a wizard step (details, prompts, competitors, owned_media) with strict forward gating; responds with next-step AI suggestions.",
        "operationId": "updateProjectDraft",
        "x-mcp-tool": "update_project_draft",
        "x-write": true,
        "description": "Submit one step (details, prompts, competitors, owned_media). Strict forward gating: a step is only accepted when every previous step is complete (`ERR_DRAFT_STATE` otherwise); completed steps can be resubmitted. Responds with the updated draft plus AI suggestions for the next step.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "step"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "step": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "enum": [
                      "details",
                      "prompts",
                      "competitors",
                      "owned_media"
                    ]
                  },
                  "name": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "brand_name": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "description": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "industry": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  },
                  "matching_names": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  },
                  "external_identifier": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "prompts": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    "maxItems": 100
                  },
                  "competitors": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "object"
                    }
                  },
                  "youtube_channel_url": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "instagram_profile_url": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "facebook_page_url": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "tiktok_profile_url": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "app_store_url": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "google_play_url": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "suggest": {
                    "type": "boolean",
                    "default": true
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Draft envelope with next-step suggestions"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/KeyProjectScoped"
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
          },
          "422": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/UnprocessableEntity"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/project_drafts/{id}/finalize": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "Projects"
        ],
        "summary": "Finalize a draft into a real project",
        "x-llms-description": "Create the real project from a completed draft (idempotent; same effects as POST /projects).",
        "operationId": "finalizeProjectDraft",
        "x-mcp-tool": "finalize_project_draft",
        "x-write": true,
        "description": "Creates the project with all accumulated draft data (same effects as POST /projects). Idempotent: finalizing an already-finalized draft returns 200 with the existing project. Optional overrides: weekly_email_subscribed, execute_prompts_immediately.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": false,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "weekly_email_subscribed": {
                    "type": "boolean"
                  },
                  "execute_prompts_immediately": {
                    "type": "boolean"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "Project created",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProjectCreateResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "200": {
            "description": "Idempotent replay"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/KeyProjectScoped"
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
          },
          "422": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/UnprocessableEntity"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/projects": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "Projects"
        ],
        "summary": "Create a project (fast mode)",
        "x-llms-description": "Create a complete project in one call (name, locale, prompts, competitors, owned media, Brand Book profile); idempotent via external_identifier.",
        "operationId": "createProject",
        "x-mcp-tool": "create_project",
        "x-write": true,
        "description": "Create a complete project in one call: project fields, prompts (queued for execution and categorization), collections tagging those prompts, competitors, weekly email subscription. The response lists same_domain_projects so an accidental duplicate is visible; it never blocks the create. Idempotent via `external_identifier` (embed-enabled accounts only; replay returns 200 with the existing project). Requires a `read_write` scope API key.",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProjectCreateRequest"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "Created",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProjectCreateResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "200": {
            "description": "Idempotent replay (existing external_identifier)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProjectCreateResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/KeyProjectScoped"
          },
          "422": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/UnprocessableEntity"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/projects/{id}": {
      "patch": {
        "tags": [
          "Projects"
        ],
        "summary": "Update a project profile (Brand Book)",
        "x-llms-description": "Update the project profile / Brand Book (brand_name, description, industry, business_model, target_audience, brand_voice, goals, primary_products, matching_names) and, account owner only, additional_owned_domains. A matching_names or additional_owned_domains change reprocesses past answers in the background.",
        "operationId": "updateProject",
        "x-mcp-tool": "update_project",
        "x-write": true,
        "description": "Updates the project name and profile, the same fields as Project Settings: name, brand_name, description, industry, business_model (plus business_model_other when it is OTHER), target_audience, brand_voice, goals, primary_products, matching_names, and the additional owned domains (additional_owned_domains). Send only the fields to change; unknown fields are rejected, and a request is applied whole or not at all. All seven Brand Book fields feed every GEO Writer task and prompt suggestions; only industry, description, and target_audience help Recommendations. A matching_names change re-runs mention/citation matching over the project history in the background, and an additional_owned_domains change reprocesses the past answers that cite an added or removed domain (rematching=true); further edits are rejected while that runs. Only the account owner can send additional_owned_domains: a team member key gets ERR_INSUFFICIENT_PERMISSION and nothing is applied. Requires a `read_write` scope API key.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "integer"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "name": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Project name shown in the app. A label: it does not change mention detection unless brand_name is empty. Cannot be blank"
                  },
                  "brand_name": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Brand name used to detect mentions. Applies to future runs; it does not rewrite history"
                  },
                  "description": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "What the brand does. Context for Recommendations and GEO Writer (Brand Book)"
                  },
                  "industry": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Single industry key (e.g. SAAS), stored as sent; an array of keys is also accepted and stored as an array, like the in-app multi-select. Unknown keys are rejected with the valid keys listed"
                  },
                  "business_model": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Business model key (e.g. B2B_SAAS); unknown keys are rejected"
                  },
                  "business_model_other": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Free-text business model, only accepted when business_model is OTHER; rejected against any other key"
                  },
                  "target_audience": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Who the brand sells to (Brand Book)"
                  },
                  "brand_voice": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Tone of voice guidance for generated content (Brand Book)"
                  },
                  "goals": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "What the brand wants to achieve. Context for GEO Writer and prompt suggestions"
                  },
                  "primary_products": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    "description": "Full replacement list of the main products or services"
                  },
                  "matching_names": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    "description": "FULL replacement list of the brand-name variants used to detect mentions; send every variant to keep"
                  },
                  "additional_owned_domains": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    "description": "FULL replacement list (at most 10) of other domains the brand owns, such as a blog or a country site; [] clears it. Citations from them count as owned, like the project website. Each entry is a website's own domain and covers its subdomains; a pasted URL is stored as its domain (https://www.acme.co.uk/x becomes acme.co.uk). A list the domain editor would refuse (a subdomain such as blog.acme.com, a platform many companies share such as youtube.com, amazon.com or wordpress.com, the project website, a tracked competitor domain, a duplicate or an entry that is not a domain) is rejected with ERR_INVALID_PARAM and the reason. Order does not matter, and an unchanged list starts nothing. Account owner only, on every plan"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Updated",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProjectUpdateResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "A write with a read-only key answers ERR_INSUFFICIENT_SCOPE. A team member whose permissions do not grant Projects update, or who sends additional_owned_domains, answers ERR_INSUFFICIENT_PERMISSION, with the same status",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": {
                    "code": "ERR_INSUFFICIENT_PERMISSION",
                    "message": "insufficient_team_member_permission"
                  },
                  "request_id": "abc-123"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
          },
          "422": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/UnprocessableEntity"
          }
        }
      }
    },
